      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1: why is a write harder than a read?"
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 1 of 8: why writes are harder"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "why"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "On a read, the cache reads the data and checks the tag at the same time. On a miss, it just throws the data away."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[0][1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A write cannot do that. If the tag does not match, writing first would destroy another block's data. So the tag check comes first, and a write hit takes longer."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[0][2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A write may also change just one byte of a block, so the cache must change exactly those bytes."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And after a write, the cache holds a newer value than memory. When does memory catch up? That is the policy."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "the question: when does memory get the new value?"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "wt",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2: write-through. Here is a CPU, a two line cache, and memory holding blocks A, B and C."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 2 of 8: write-through"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "why"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "path"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "c1"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "m1"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Line 0 holds block A, with the value 10. Memory also says 10. They agree."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "c1[0]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "m1[0][1]",
       "delay": 0.25
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The CPU writes 11 to A. It is a hit, so the cache line changes to 11."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "path.cpu"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "path.cpu->cache",
       "delay": 0.25
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "path.cache",
       "delay": 0.5
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "c1[0][4]",
       "value": "11",
       "delay": 0.6
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Write-through sends the same write on to memory at once. Memory becomes 11 too."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "path.cache->mem"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "path.mem",
       "delay": 0.25
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "m1[0][1]",
       "value": "11",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Now 12, then 13. Every write goes to the cache and to memory."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "c1[0][4]",
       "value": "12"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "m1[0][1]",
       "value": "12",
       "delay": 0.2
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "c1[0][4]",
       "value": "13",
       "delay": 0.5
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "m1[0][1]",
       "value": "13",
       "delay": 0.7
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "path.cache->mem",
       "delay": 0.1
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Memory always holds the latest value, so a line never needs to be written back. The dirty bit is not needed: shown as a dash."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "c1.dirty"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The cost: three writes made three trips to memory. Memory takes around 100 cycles, so if the CPU waited each time, every store would cost 100 cycles."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "write-through: every write goes to memory · memory is always current"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "buffer",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 3: so write-through caches add a write buffer between the cache and memory."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 3 of 8: the write buffer"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "path"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "c1"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "m1"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "pathb"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "buf"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The CPU writes A equals 11 into the cache and into the buffer, and carries on with its next instruction straight away."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pathb.cpu->cache"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pathb.cache->buf",
       "delay": 0.25
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "buf[0]",
       "value": "A=11",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "More writes arrive: B equals 21, A equals 12, C equals 31. Each takes a slot."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "buf[1]",
       "value": "B=21"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "buf[2]",
       "value": "A=12",
       "delay": 0.3
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "buf[3]",
       "value": "C=31",
       "delay": 0.6
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Meanwhile, the buffer drains to memory in the background, oldest first. A equals 11 goes out, and its slot frees up."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pathb.buf->mem"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pathb.mem",
       "delay": 0.25
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "buf[0]",
       "value": "",
       "delay": 0.6
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "But if writes come faster than memory can take them, the buffer fills, and then the CPU must stall."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "buf[0]",
       "value": "B=22"
      },
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "buf[0..=3]",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Here are the four rules of a write buffer."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "pathb"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "buf"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "bufx"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "bufx[0..=1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A full buffer stalls the CPU. And a trap: if a read misses on a block whose new value is still waiting in the buffer, memory has the old value."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "bufx[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "bufx[3]",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "So the read must check the buffer first, or wait for it to drain. Otherwise it reads stale data."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "write buffer: the CPU does not wait · full buffer → stall · read misses check it"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "wb",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 4: write-back. Same machine, but now each line has a dirty bit, and memory is updated only when a line is evicted."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 4 of 8: write-back and the dirty bit"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "bufx"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "path"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "c2"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "m2"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Line 0 holds A equals 10, dirty bit 0, which means clean: the same as memory."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "c2[0]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "c2[0][2]",
       "delay": 0.25
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The CPU writes 11 to A. The cache changes to 11, and the dirty bit is set to 1."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "path.cpu->cache"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "path.cache",
       "delay": 0.25
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "c2[0][4]",
       "value": "11",
       "delay": 0.4
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "c2[0][2]",
       "value": "1",
       "delay": 0.7
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Memory is not touched. It still says 10. The cache and memory now disagree, and the dirty bit records that."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "m2[0][1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "c2[0][2]",
       "delay": 0.3
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Writes of 12 and 13 change only the cache. Three writes, zero trips to memory."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "c2[0][4]",
       "value": "12"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "c2[0][4]",
       "value": "13",
       "delay": 0.5
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "c2[0][4]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Now the CPU reads C. C also maps to line 0, so it is a miss, and A must be evicted."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "c2[0]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "m2[0][3]",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A is dirty, so before C can come in, the whole block A is written back. Memory finally gets 13."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "path.cache->mem"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "path.mem",
       "delay": 0.25
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "m2[0][1]",
       "value": "13",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then C is fetched into line 0, clean, with the value 30."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "c2[0][3]",
       "value": "C"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "c2[0][4]",
       "value": "30",
       "delay": 0.3
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "c2[0][2]",
       "value": "0",
       "delay": 0.6
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "c2[0]",
       "delay": 0.6
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Later, if C is evicted while still clean, it is just dropped: memory already has the same value. Only dirty blocks cost a write back."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "write-back: write the cache only · dirty bit · write the block back on eviction"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Edge case: the dirty bit is per line, not per byte. Change one byte, and the whole block goes back to memory."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "c2.dirty"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "wmiss",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 5: so far every write was a hit. What if the block is not in the cache?"
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 5 of 8: write misses"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "c2"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "m2"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "c3"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "m3"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Line 0 holds A. The CPU writes 31 to C, which maps to line 0: a write miss."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "c3[0]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "m3[0][3]",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Choice one, write-allocate: treat it like a read miss. Fetch C into line 0, then write 31 into the cache."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "c3[0][3]",
       "value": "C"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "c3[0][4]",
       "value": "30",
       "delay": 0.3
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "c3[0][4]",
       "value": "31",
       "delay": 0.7
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "path.cache->mem"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Next time the CPU touches C, it hits."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "c3[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Choice two, no-write-allocate: go around the cache. Put C back the way it was, with A in line 0."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "c3[0][3]",
       "value": "A"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "c3[0][4]",
       "value": "10",
       "delay": 0.3
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The write of 31 goes straight to memory, and the cache does not change. Also called write-around."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "path.cache->mem"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "m3[0][3]",
       "value": "31",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Which pairs make sense?"
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "path"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "c3"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "m3"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "pairs"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pairs[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Write-back goes with write-allocate: bring the block in, and later writes to it hit and stay in the cache."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pairs[1][1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Write-through goes with no-write-allocate: every write goes to memory anyway, so fetching the block would only add traffic."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pairs[1][2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Write-allocate pays off when the block is used again soon. No-write-allocate pays off for data written once, like clearing a large array."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pairs[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "write-back + write-allocate · write-through + no-write-allocate"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "traffic",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 6: one trace, both pairs. X and Y map to the same line of a direct-mapped cache, which starts empty."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 6 of 8: counting the traffic"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "pairs"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "traffic"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Access 1, write X, misses. Write-back with allocate fetches X, writes it in the cache, and sets dirty."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "traffic[0]"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[0][2]",
       "value": "miss: fetch X, write, dirty"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[0][3]",
       "value": "1 block read",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Write-through with no allocate sends the word to memory and leaves the cache empty."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[0][4]",
       "value": "miss: write word to memory"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[0][5]",
       "value": "1 word write",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Access 2, write X again. Write-back: now a hit, the cache changes, memory does not."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "traffic[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[1][2]",
       "value": "hit: write in cache"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[1][3]",
       "value": "none",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Write-through: X was never brought in, so a miss again, and another word to memory."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[1][4]",
       "value": "miss: write word to memory"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[1][5]",
       "value": "1 word write",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Access 3, read X. Write-back: a hit."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "traffic[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[2][2]",
       "value": "hit"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[2][3]",
       "value": "none",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Write-through: a read miss, so now X is fetched into the cache."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[2][4]",
       "value": "miss: fetch X"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[2][5]",
       "value": "1 block read",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Access 4, write Y, same line. Write-back: a miss; dirty X must be written back, then Y fetched."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "traffic[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[3][2]",
       "value": "miss: write back X, fetch Y, dirty"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[3][3]",
       "value": "1 block write + 1 block read",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Write-through: a miss, the word goes to memory, and X stays in the cache."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[3][4]",
       "value": "miss: write word to memory"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[3][5]",
       "value": "1 word write",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Access 5, read X. Write-back: X was evicted, so a miss; dirty Y goes back, then X is fetched."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "traffic[4]"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[4][2]",
       "value": "miss: write back Y, fetch X"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[4][3]",
       "value": "1 block write + 1 block read",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Write-through: X is still there, a hit."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[4][4]",
       "value": "hit"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "traffic[4][5]",
       "value": "none",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Add up each column."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "traffic"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "tsum"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Write-back: block reads at accesses 1, 4 and 5 make 3; block writes at 4 and 5 make 2; no single-word writes."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "tsum[0][1]",
       "value": "3"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "tsum[0][2]",
       "value": "2",
       "delay": 0.4
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "tsum[0][3]",
       "value": "0",
       "delay": 0.7
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "tsum[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Write-through: one block read at access 3, and single-word writes at 1, 2 and 4: 3."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "tsum[1][1]",
       "value": "1"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "tsum[1][2]",
       "value": "0",
       "delay": 0.4
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "tsum[1][3]",
       "value": "3",
       "delay": 0.7
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "tsum[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Neither always wins. Write-back moves whole blocks, but rarely. Write-through moves small words, but often."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "write-back: few, large transfers · write-through: many, small ones"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "costs",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 7: putting numbers on the costs."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 7 of 8: costs in cycles and bytes"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "tsum"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "cost"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "With write-back, a miss sometimes has to write a dirty block back first. If a fraction f of evicted blocks are dirty, the average miss penalty is 1 plus f, times the block transfer time."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cost[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "With 30 percent dirty and 100 cycles per block, a miss costs 130 cycles on average, not 100."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "cost[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cost[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Traffic in bytes: a million 4 byte writes under write-through send 4 megabytes to memory."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "cost[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cost[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Under write-back, suppose those writes cause 20 thousand dirty evictions of 64 byte blocks: 1.28 megabytes. Much less, when writes hit the same blocks again and again."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "cost[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cost[3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Here is everything side by side."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "cost"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "cmp"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cmp[0..=1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Read misses cost more under write-back, because a dirty victim must go first. Repeated writes cost far less."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cmp[2..=3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And with several processors or DMA devices sharing memory, write-back means memory can be stale. That needs cache coherence, a later topic."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cmp[4]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "most modern caches: write-back + write-allocate, with a write buffer for the evictions"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "exam",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Now an exam question."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Exam question"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "cmp"
